The `getRobotCoordinate` method retrieves the current coordinate of a specified robot ID. The `setRobotCoordinate` method modifies the coordinates of a specific robot, ensuring that thread safety is maintained without explicit synchronization using the `synchronized` keyword. It only succeeds if the robot ID already exists in the map.

Two versions of the `getLiveRobotCoordinates` method are provided: one returns a live unmodifiable view backed by the original data (the ConcurrentHashMap itself), and the other returns a static snapshot of the current state as an unmodifiable map using `ConcurrentHashMap.entrySet().stream().collect(Collectors.toMap(Map.Entry::getKey, Map.Entry::getValue))`.

